  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## How to activate a population of cells\n",
    "\n",
    "We can test the effects of activating different cell populations, like we might through optogenetics in vivo. \n",
    "\n",
    "Let's start with activating PV neurons in the model. We will first get the node ID of each PV (or Pvalb) neuron in the V1 network to tell the simulator which nodes to activate. "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "net = pu.form_network('output/config.json')\n",
    "\n",
    "v1df = net.nodes[\"v1\"].to_dataframe()\n",
    "v1df = pu.pick_core(v1df, radius=radius)\n",
    "v1df[\"Cell Type\"] = v1df[\"pop_name\"].apply(pu.identify_cell_type)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "PV_node_ids = v1df[(v1df['Cell Type']=='Pvalb') & (v1df['layer']=='L5')]['node_id'].sort_values()+1 # nest ids start at 1 not 0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We will now make a new configuration file with added instructions to provide an additional input current to all PV neurons in the model. For convenience, we will use the configuration file from our first drifting grating simulation as a template. Additional documentation on providing a current clamp stimulus to the model is available on the [BMTK website](https://alleninstitute.github.io/bmtk/current_clamps.html)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import json \n",
    "\n",
    "config_template = 'v1_point_config/config.json'\n",
    "\n",
    "config_js = json.load(open(config_template))\n",
    "\n",
    "# create a new output directory\n",
    "output_dir = 'output_PV_clamp'\n",
    "os.makedirs(output_dir, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "config_js[\"manifest\"][\"$OUTPUT_DIR\"] = output_dir\n",
    "config_js[\"inputs\"][\"current_clamp\"] = {}\n",
    "config_js[\"inputs\"][\"current_clamp\"][\"module\"] = \"IClamp\"\n",
    "config_js[\"inputs\"][\"current_clamp\"][\"input_type\"] = \"current_clamp\"\n",
    "config_js[\"inputs\"][\"current_clamp\"][\"node_set\"] = PV_node_ids.to_list()\n",
    "config_js[\"inputs\"][\"current_clamp\"][\"amp\"] = 1000.0 # pA\n",
    "config_js[\"inputs\"][\"current_clamp\"][\"delay\"] = 500.0 # ms\n",
    "config_js[\"inputs\"][\"current_clamp\"][\"duration\"] = 2500.0 # ms\n",
    "\n",
    "config_name = 'v1_point_config/config_PV_clamp.json'\n",
    "\n",
    "json.dump(config_js, open(config_name, \"w\"), indent = 2)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from run_pointnet import main as run_pointnet\n",
    "\n",
    "pointnet_config_clamp = 'v1_point_config/config_PV_clamp.json'\n",
    "run_pointnet(pointnet_config_clamp)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Let's plot a raster plot to visualize the results of the simulation:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "pointnet_config = 'output_PV_clamp/config_PV_clamp.json'\n",
    "net = 'full'\n",
    "sortby='tuning_angle'\n",
    "radius = 400.0\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n",
    "\n",
    "ax = pu.plot_raster(pointnet_config, sortby=sortby, **pu.settings[net])\n",
    "ax.set_xlim([0, 3000])\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "config_folder = os.path.dirname(pointnet_config)\n",
    "plt.savefig(f\"{config_folder}/raster_by_{sortby}.png\", dpi=300)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "spikes_df, hue_order, color_dict, layer_divisions = pu.make_figure_elements(pointnet_config, radius, sortby)\n",
    "\n",
    "rates = spikes_df[spikes_df['timestamps']>500.0].groupby(['Sorted ID'])['timestamps'].count()/2.5\n",
    "rates = rates.reset_index(name = 'Mean Rate')\n",
    "rates_df = spikes_df[['population', 'Sorted ID', 'Cell Type', 'Tuning Angle', 'layer']].drop_duplicates('Sorted ID')\n",
    "rates_df = rates_df.merge(rates, how='left', left_on='Sorted ID', right_on = 'Sorted ID')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "rates_df[rates_df['Cell Type']=='Pvalb']"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
