   "source": [
    "## Compute OSI and DSI\n",
    "\n",
    "A common metric in visual neuroscience is the orientation selectivity index (OSI) and direction selectivity index (DSI) of a population of cells in V1. These metrics measure how much a cell prefers to fire in response to a grating at one orientation versus another, or the response of a grating moving in one direction more than another. \n",
    "\n",
    "We pre-ran the simulations necessary to calculate OSI and DSI for the model in the folder **output_all_directions**. There is model output from 10 trials at 8 different orientations. \n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
